From e5ec561ed1f67dc5f107b7a6def095a876e24f93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek <abhishek01789@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:32:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/41] Slide plasmashell popups out of their panel, like
 KWin's sliding popups

- Kickoff, the calendar, tray popups and the grouped-window list slide
  152 px out of the panel they belong to, fading when taller than that
- 200 ms times AnimationDurationFactor 0.25 = 50 ms, OutCubic in, InCubic
  out (KWin's OutCubic backwards); the popup stays drawn while closing
- Moved through the rect, so the blur behind follows the popup
- plasmashell runs with KDE_FULL_SESSION=true and KDE_SESSION_VERSION=6 so
  KDE libraries apply full-session behaviour (tray icon colours)
- debug.slidingPopups IPC slows the slide for tests
